#' Provenance of the bundled reference data
#'
#' Every table shipped with tidybrreg is listed here with its source,
#' licence, vintage, the transformations applied, and how the package
#' uses it. The tables are regenerated by `data-raw/build_dictionaries.R`;
#' the vintages below are the dates of the last regeneration that
#' touched each table, taken from the repository history.
#'
#' @section Exported datasets (`data/`):
#' \describe{
#'   \item{[field_dict]}{**Package-authored.** A mapping from BRREG JSON
#'     paths and CSV column headers to English column names and R
#'     types, written by the package author from the Enhetsregisteret
#'     API documentation (<https://data.brreg.no/enhetsregisteret/api/dokumentasjon/>)
#'     and from fields observed on live responses. The Norwegian paths
#'     are BRREG's identifiers; the English names and types are the
#'     author's editorial choices and carry the package's MIT licence.
#'     Last revised 2026-06-16. Used at runtime by every parser.}
#'   \item{[legal_forms]}{**BRREG code list plus manual translation.**
#'     `code`, `name_no` and `expired` are retrieved from
#'     `GET https://data.brreg.no/enhetsregisteret/api/organisasjonsformer`,
#'     published by the Brønnøysund Register Centre under the Norwegian
#'     Licence for Open Government Data (NLOD) 2.0
#'     (<https://data.norge.no/nlod/en/2.0>); `name_en` is a manual
#'     translation by the package author (unreviewed by BRREG), falling
#'     back to `name_no` for codes without a translation. Retrieved
#'     2026-06-16. Used by [brreg_label()].}
#'   \item{[role_types]}{**Package-authored from BRREG documentation.**
#'     Codes and Norwegian descriptions follow the role codes listed in
#'     the Enhetsregisteret roller documentation and the Fullmakt
#'     service; English names are a manual translation by the package
#'     author. BRREG publishes no machine-readable role code list with
#'     translations. Last revised 2026-06-16. Used by [brreg_roles()],
#'     [brreg_roles_legal()], [brreg_signatur()], [brreg_prokura()] and
#'     [brreg_label()].}
#'   \item{[role_groups]}{**Package-authored from BRREG documentation.**
#'     As [role_types], for role group (`rollegruppe`) codes. Last
#'     revised 2026-06-16. Used by [brreg_roles()] and [brreg_label()].}
#' }
#'
#' @section Internal fallback dictionaries (`R/sysdata.rda`):
#' \describe{
#'   \item{`nace_codes`}{**Statistics Norway (SSB) KLASS classification
#'     6** (Standard Industrial Classification SN2007), English labels,
#'     retrieved from `https://data.ssb.no/api/klass/v1/classifications/6/codesAt`
#'     on 2026-06-16 (the effective date of the codes is that retrieval
#'     date). SSB publishes KLASS classifications as open data under
#'     NLOD 2.0 according to its data licence page
#'     (<https://www.ssb.no/en/omssb/tjenester-og-verktoy/api/klass-api>);
#'     the maintainer has not obtained a separate confirmation, so the
#'     statement is reproduced as published. Used only when SSB KLASS
#'     is unreachable or `source = "bundled"` is requested in
#'     [get_brreg_dic()]; the returned tibble carries `vintage`.}
#'   \item{`sector_codes`}{**SSB KLASS classification 39** (institutional
#'     sector), English labels, same source, licence statement,
#'     retrieval date and use as `nace_codes`.}
#' }
#'
#' @section Register data:
#' Entity, role, group, signature and update data retrieved at runtime
#' come from the Brønnøysund Register Centre's open APIs and are
#' licensed under NLOD 2.0; the licence requires attribution to the
#' Brønnøysund Register Centre when the data are redistributed. KLASS
#' labels retrieved at runtime are Statistics Norway's.
#'
#' @name tidybrreg_provenance
#' @family tidybrreg reference data
NULL

#' Field dictionary: Norwegian API paths to English column names
#'
#' A tibble mapping brreg JSON field paths to English column names and
#' R types. Used internally by the parse engine. API fields absent from
#' this dictionary pass through with auto-generated snake_case names
#' rather than being silently dropped. A few fields appear twice because
#' the JSON API and the CSV bulk spell them differently
#' (`registreringsdatoEnhetsregisteret` /
#' `registreringsdatoIEnhetsregisteret`); the first observed spelling
#' takes the English name and a second one, if ever observed in the same
#' payload, keeps its snake_case name.
#'
#' @format A tibble with 103 rows and 3 columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{api_path}{Dot-notation path in the brreg JSON response
#'     (e.g. `"organisasjonsnummer"`, `"forretningsadresse.kommune"`).}
#'   \item{col_name}{English column name used in package output
#'     (e.g. `"org_nr"`, `"municipality"`).}
#'   \item{type}{R type for coercion: `"character"`, `"Date"`,
#'     `"integer"`, `"numeric"`, or `"logical"`.}
#' }
#'
#' @source Package-authored; see [tidybrreg_provenance].
#' @family tidybrreg reference data
#' @seealso [brreg_entity()] for the function that uses this dictionary.
#'
#' @examples
#' field_dict
#' field_dict[field_dict$type == "Date", ]
"field_dict"

#' Norwegian legal form codes with English translations
#'
#' All organisasjonsformer registered with the Brønnøysund Register
#' Centre, with English translations. Codes and Norwegian names are
#' fetched from the brreg API during package build; the English names
#' are manual translations by the package author.
#'
#' @format A tibble with 44 rows and 4 columns:
#' \describe{
#'   \item{code}{Legal form code (e.g. `"AS"`, `"ASA"`, `"ENK"`).}
#'   \item{name_no}{Norwegian description.}
#'   \item{expired}{Date string if the form is expired, `NA` otherwise.}
#'   \item{name_en}{English translation.}
#' }
#'
#' @source Brønnøysund Register Centre,
#'   <https://data.brreg.no/enhetsregisteret/api/organisasjonsformer>,
#'   NLOD 2.0, retrieved 2026-06-16; see [tidybrreg_provenance].
#' @family tidybrreg reference data
#' @seealso [brreg_label()] to translate legal form codes in entity data.
#'
#' @examples
#' legal_forms
#' legal_forms[legal_forms$code == "AS", ]
"legal_forms"

